# .npmignore — secondary gate for `npm pack`.
#
# The `files` whitelist in package.json is the PRIMARY gate (it
# whitelists the runtime files we want shipped). This file is the
# secondary gate: it controls what `npm pack` excludes when the
# whitelist happens to match something we don't want. Notably, npm's
# "always include README variants" rule pulls in `scripts/README.md`
# even though it's not in the whitelist — this file tells npm to
# drop it.

# Documentation in scripts/ — only the runtime scripts (tts-minimax,
# tts-openai, fw-openai-sts) and install.sh should ship. The README
# is for the dev tools (dev-status.sh, dev-watch.sh) which are NOT
# in the npm package; they stay in the repo for development only.
scripts/README.md
